tle":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"184.147.121.183","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":75396,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"34113b2bd961b05c0f897206b3bc71e7","RawContent":"I started with mywedding.com and ended up using weddingwire.com. \n\n\nI still have no colour scheme and am not sure I want anything other than neutral colours with maybe a pop of sparkle. Finding a specific colour scheme to match was not necessary (obviously) but I was able to find one with a calligraphy font I loved that matched our save the dates. \n\n\nI caution you to make your site name as short as possible. We had a longer one that didn&#039;t fit well in most STDs. Of coarse you could pay for your domain too if that&#039;s important to you. We decided to keep the $50-$60 and spend it on other (likely unnecessary) things lol","Attachments":[],"Id":1896846,"PostDate":1432260665,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                I started with mywedding.com and ended up using weddingwire.com. <br><br>\nI still have no colour scheme and am not sure I want anything other than neutral colours with maybe a pop of sparkle. Finding a specific colour scheme to match was not necessary (obviously) but I was able to find one with a calligraphy font I loved that matched our save the dates. <br><br>\nI caution you to make your site name as short as possible. We had a longer one that didn't fit well in most STDs. Of coarse y