Request Time: 0 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":31160,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"e2e430100028cf9d5f0aa6da3e52cdfd","RawContent":"&lt;div style=\"margin:20px; margin-top:5px; \"&gt; &lt;div class=\"smallfont\"&gt;Quote:&lt;\/div&gt; &lt;table cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" width=\"99%\"&gt; &lt;tr&gt; &lt;td class=\"alt2\" style=\"border:1px inset\"&gt;  Originally Posted by &lt;strong&gt;San Fran Sarah&lt;\/strong&gt; &lt;img class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"View Post\"&gt;  &lt;div style=\"font-style:italic\"&gt;Jacilynda--thanks for the helpful hints. I bought my LEDs and batteries but I haven&#039;t gotten around to making them yet. Did you only need 1 battery for each lantern or did you need 1 battery for each LED?\n Did you try the on\/off switch?&lt;\/div&gt; &lt;\/td&gt; &lt;\/tr&gt; &lt;\/table&gt; &lt;\/div&gt;I only used one led per battery. i didn&#039;t think of 2 per battery. I didnt do the on off switch. I just took the tape off after the photo and took them apart. I&#039;m sooo pleased! Thanks Sarah! I wasn&#039;t going to like them before, and just let them hang for color, but now they will be so much fun when it gets dark.","Attachments":[],"Id":614127,"PostDate":1236461407,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <div  style=\"margin:20px\"> <div class=\"smallfont\">Quote:<\/div> <table cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" width=\"99%\"> <tr> <td class=\"alt2\" style=\"border:1px inset\">  Originally Posted by <strong>San Fran Sarah<\/strong> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"View Post\"><\/span>  <div  style=\"font-style:italic\">Jacilynda--thanks for the helpful hints. I bought my LEDs and batteries but I haven't gotten around to making them yet. Did you only need 1 battery for each lantern or did you need 1 battery for each LED?<br \/> Did you try the on\/off switch?<\/div> <\/td> <\/tr> <\/table> <\/div>I only used one led per battery. i didn't think of 2 per battery. I didnt do the on off switch. I just took the tape off after the photo and took them apart. I'm sooo pleased! Thanks Sarah! I wasn't going to like them before, and just let them hang for color, but now they will be so much fun when it gets dark.\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><span>Photo by <\/span><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/www.dlweddings.com\">www.dlweddings.com<\/a><br><br><span>My Planning Thread<\/span><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/bestdestinationwedding.com\/forum\/t46588\">http:\/\/bestdestinationwedding.com\/forum\/t46588<\/a><span>My Wedding Review w\/ Lots of Pics<\/span><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/bestdestinationwedding.com\/forum\/t48352\">http:\/\/bestdestinationwedding.com\/forum\/t48352<\/a><span>Our TTD pics<\/span><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/bestdestinationwedding.com\/forum\/t48445\">http:\/\/bestdestinationwedding.com\/forum\/t48445<\/a><\/div><\/div>","Email":"jacilyn.m.gannon@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1212460200,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewrig