226801,"Name":"futur_bride","IsOnline":false}},"Posts":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":true,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":51182,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"b43cc0745ca17a1b267d412dedeff4b6","RawContent":"Hey everybody,\n \n Yesterday, I start working on my DIY aisle runner. I&#039;ve look on internet and it was tooooooo expensive for me. So I decide to do one by myself.\n \n My aisle runner is brown and the petals are tiffany blue. I have a turquoise rubbon that I glue all around it.\n \n The first step was to do the monogram! OUFFF! It was suuuuper long. Because my aisle was brown and I had to paint it 2 times to have the color that I want.\n \n The second step was to glue the rubbon. I start using fabric glue but it&#039;s scrap... It is long to dry. So we change for glue gun. BETTER!\n \n The final step was to glue the petals. I&#039;m currently doing it. I have to glue around 4000 petals! &lt;img src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/fencing.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Fencing\" class=\"inlineimg\" \/&gt; Really tricky! But I have a wonderful boyfriend that is helping me glue all the petals! \n \n Picture are coming for tonight! PROMISE! &lt;img src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/smile123.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile123\" class=\"inlineimg\" \/&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1127637,"PostDate":1272220184,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Hey everybody,<br \/> <br \/> Yesterday, I start working on my DIY aisle runner. I've look on internet and it was tooooooo expensive for me. So I decide to do one by myself.<br \/> <br \/> My aisle runner is brown and the petals are tiffany blue. I have a turquoise rubbon that I glue all around it.<br \/> <br \/> The first step was to do the monogram! OUFFF! It was suuuuper long. Because my aisle was brown and I had to paint it 2 times to have the color that I want.<br \/> <br \/> The second step was to glue the rubbon. I start using fabric glue but it's scrap... It is long to dry. So we change for glue gun. BETTER!<br \/> <br \/> The final step was to glue the petals. I'm currently doing it. I have to glue around 4000 petals! <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/fencing.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Fencing\" class=\"inlineimg\" \/><\/span> Really tricky! But I have a wonderful boyfriend that is helping me glue all the petals! <br \/> <br \/> Picture are coming for tonight! PROMISE! <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/smile123.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile123\" class=\"inlineimg\" \/><\/span>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><span>RIVIERA MAYA 2011<\/span><br><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/t\/wxXZqCZ\/weight.png\">http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt...qCZ\/weight.png<\/a><br><br><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10732;128\/st\/20110412\/e\/Our+Wedding+in+Paradise%21\/k\/e320\/event.png\">http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt...e320\/event.png<\/a><\/div><\/div>","Email":"cberg008@uottawa.ca","IpAddress":""